and instruction manuals; and devices that deliver neuromodulation therapy for treating drug-resistant epilepsy and depression. This segment also includes the development and clinical testing of aura6000 system for treating obstructive sleep apnea. It serves perfusionists, neurologists, neurosurgeons, hospitals, other healthcare professionals and medical institutions, and healthcare providers. The company sells its medical devices through direct sales representatives, agents, and independent distributors in the United States, the United Kingdom, Germany, France, Italy, the Netherlands, Spain, Belgium, Poland, Sweden, Switzerland, Austria, Norway, Portugal, Finland, Denmark, and internationally. LivaNova PLC was incorporated in 2015 and is headquartered in Gloucester, the United Kingdom.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Vladimir A. Makatsaria | CEO & Director | Age 52 | Compensation: $2.4M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 3K people. Revenue per employee of $421K ranks in the above the sector median among Healthcare peers. Each employee generates $53K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $11K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 6\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["LivaNova PLC is a mid-cap healthcare business with a $5.0B market cap on $1.4B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +11% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at -0% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 68% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $173M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 12 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage runs at 4.0\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 1.6\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 217% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":2.167607269791124},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (13.3% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 15% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% o